    s_users_create_conns_help: 'Off (the default), only the administrator creates connections, in Administration → Connections, and users use the ones given to them. Those they already had stay: they can use them, adjust their options and delete them, but not change the computer they go to.',
    s_kerberos_rc4: 'Allow Kerberos with RC4 (Windows Server 2003 domains)',
    s_kerberos_rc4_help: 'Security risk: turn it on only if you need it. It is needed for a Windows Server 2003 domain or an account whose password is older than its domain\'s AES keys; without it, those accounts sign in with NTLM. It is not needed to connect to Windows XP: those computers use Standard RDP Security, without Kerberos. With RC4, someone on the network between this server and the domain controller can pose as it and get something to try passwords against on their own computer thousands of times faster than with AES.',
